---
title: How-to packs
description: "How-to packs: pictures, a video link, three cues and the common mistake for exercises, which coaches show their clients. Data only."
---

A how-to pack gives exercises a how-to: pictures, a video, three cues and the most common
mistake. Coaches add it in Coaching › Plugins › How-to packs. Their own how-tos come first; a
pack's fill in the exercises they haven't written one for, and LogIt's cover the rest. The
how-tos go to their clients with the programs that use those exercises, and show on the client's
Home before their first session and under **How to** in the workout.

A pack is data only: installing one asks nothing and it runs no code.

## howtos.json

```json
{
  "formatVersion": 1,
  "howtos": [
    {
      "exercise": "Kettlebell Swing",
      "pictures": ["https://example.com/swing-top.jpg", "https://example.com/swing-hinge.jpg"],
      "video": "https://youtu.be/XXXXXXXXXXX?t=12",
      "cues": ["Hips back, not down", "Snap the hips", "Arms are ropes"],
      "mistake": "Squatting the swing: keep shins nearly vertical"
    }
  ]
}
```

- `exercise`: matched to the exercise by name, ignoring case.
- `pictures`: up to four `https` links.
- `video`: a YouTube or Vimeo link, with a start time if you like (`?t=12`). Anything else is
  refused. It plays inside LogIt only when tapped: YouTube's privacy-enhanced player, Vimeo with
  do-not-track.
- `cues`: up to three, 140 characters each. `mistake`: up to 200.
- Up to 200 how-tos in a pack.
